"""Original operational security concepts and practices."""
ITEMS=[]
def group(options,rows):
 for k,(stem,why) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((stem,[options[k]]+[o for j,o in enumerate(options) if j!=k],why))
group(['Confidentiality of the records','Integrity of the transaction','Availability of the service','Accountability for the action'],[
('A support contractor can read salary records despite having no payroll duties. The records remain accurate and the system stays online. Which security property is directly breached?', 'The issue is unauthorized disclosure. Integrity and availability may remain intact while confidentiality fails.'),
('A transfer instruction arrives with its destination account altered, even though it was never disclosed to an unauthorized reader. Which property has failed?', 'Unauthorized modification compromises integrity. Secrecy alone does not ensure that a transaction remains correct.'),
('A booking platform retains accurate, protected records but cannot serve customers during a prolonged outage. Which property is primarily affected?', 'Availability concerns timely usable access. Correct and confidential records do not help users if the service is inaccessible.'),
('All technicians share one administrative account. Changes are authorized, but investigators cannot establish which individual performed a disputed action. Which property is weakest?', 'Individual accountability requires attributable actions. A shared identity obscures the actor even when the action is otherwise permitted.')])
group(['Disclose the conflict of interest','Report the findings accurately','Seek qualified technical support','Protect entrusted information'],[
('An assessor is evaluating bids and privately owns a financial stake in one bidder. The assessment is otherwise within the assessor’s expertise. Which professional action addresses this ethical concern?', 'Disclosing the conflict allows appropriate management of impartiality. Technical competence alone does not remove a financial conflict.'),
('A project sponsor asks a tester to remove a confirmed material weakness from the final report to avoid delaying launch. Which duty governs the tester’s response?', 'Honest reporting must preserve supported material findings. A business deadline is not a reason to misrepresent the assessment.'),
('An administrator receives a specialized forensic assignment beyond their current competence. The evidence is important and the organization permits bringing in an expert. What should the administrator do?', 'Obtain qualified support rather than claim expertise they lack. Diligent service includes recognizing professional limits.'),
('A practitioner changes employers while retaining confidential design documents entrusted by the former employer. No authority permits reuse at the new company. Which duty applies to those documents?', 'Protect the entrusted information and follow authorized return or disposal requirements. Changing jobs does not grant permission to disclose it.')])
group(['Confirm the authorized scope','Use the approved escalation channel','Carry out the assigned procedure','Request an authorized exception'],[
('A technician is asked to assess a supplier system that is not listed in the signed assessment authorization. The requester cannot show supplier consent. What must be resolved before assessment activity?', 'Confirm authority and scope for the supplier system. A request from an internal colleague does not establish authorization over another party’s assets.'),
('An operator observes a suspected policy breach involving a colleague. The organization has a confidential reporting process, and no immediate safety action is required. Which route is appropriate?', 'Use the designated escalation channel with factual observations. Public accusations or private investigation beyond authority are not implied by the role.'),
('A routine backup verification task is documented, assigned to the administrator and within approved access. No exception or unexpected risk is present. What is the appropriate next action?', 'Perform the authorized procedure. Escalating every ordinary assigned task would not improve accountability or execution.'),
('A team has a legitimate need that the current access policy does not permit. The policy provides a risk-owner exception process. How should the team proceed?', 'Request a documented authorized exception instead of silently bypassing policy. A business need does not itself grant exception authority.')])
group(['A technical enforcement control','A physical access control','An administrative policy control','A personnel competence control'],[
('A service rejects connections that do not satisfy a machine-enforced network rule. Which control category best describes this mechanism?', 'Automated rule enforcement is technical. The policy authorizing the rule is administrative, but the question asks about its implementation.'),
('A secured doorway restricts entry to a room containing confidential paper records. Which control category describes the doorway mechanism?', 'The mechanism controls physical entry. A written visitor rule is a separate administrative control.'),
('Management issues a binding rule defining who may approve access exceptions. Which category describes the rule itself?', 'The policy defines organizational authority and is administrative. It does not directly act as a physical barrier or machine enforcement point.'),
('An organization gives operators role-specific practice and evaluates whether they can perform secure recovery tasks. Which control focus does this address?', 'Training and demonstrated competence prepare personnel to carry out their duties. A firewall rule cannot establish operator competence.')])
group(['Prevent the prohibited activity','Detect a completed violation','Correct the damaged condition','Compensate for a control constraint'],[
('A transaction service rejects a submission unless its required authorization is present. Which functional purpose does this control serve?', 'The control prevents the unauthorized submission from completing. A later audit would serve a detective purpose.'),
('An automated review finds that a privileged account was used outside its approved window yesterday. Which functional purpose does that review primarily serve?', 'The review detects a past violation. It did not stop the original activity from occurring.'),
('A managed process restores an accidentally altered security configuration to its approved value. Which functional purpose is being performed?', 'Restoring the approved state is corrective. Merely generating an alert would leave the altered state in place.'),
('A legacy appliance cannot support the required endpoint agent. An approved restricted gateway provides an alternative safeguard addressing the same exposure while replacement is planned. What role does that safeguard serve?', 'It compensates for a documented implementation constraint. This requires approval and evaluation rather than an assumption of automatic equivalence.')])
group(['Record the asset and its owner','Verify the acquisition requirements','Maintain the supported configuration','Authorize the final disposition'],[
('A newly discovered virtual machine processes production data, but no team accepts responsibility for it. Which lifecycle record is needed to bring it under management?', 'An accurate inventory with ownership enables accountability and subsequent control actions. Patching alone does not establish who is responsible.'),
('A department is considering a product whose support and audit capabilities may not meet policy. Which lifecycle activity belongs before purchase approval?', 'Evaluate acquisition requirements before committing to the product. A later inventory entry does not resolve unsuitable capabilities.'),
('An established application has an approved baseline and a supported patch release ready for its maintenance window. Which lifecycle activity keeps the deployed asset secure?', 'Maintain the supported configuration through the approved change process. Initial acceptance is not the end of security management.'),
('A leased device is due for return and contains organizational data. Retention requirements have been checked. Which lifecycle decision must govern its handling before release?', 'Authorized disposition specifies sanitization and release requirements. Removing the asset from the inventory alone does not protect its stored information.')])
group(['Assess the security impact','Authorize the planned change','Execute the rollback plan','Verify the post-change outcome'],[
('A proposed network change would alter access paths to a regulated service. It has not yet been approved. Which analysis should inform the approval decision?', 'Assess security impact and dependencies before authorization. A technically feasible change may still create unacceptable exposure.'),
('A tested modification has a documented impact assessment and rollback plan, but the required change owner has not agreed to production execution. Which step remains?', 'Obtain the required authorization before implementation. Successful testing does not replace the organization’s approval boundary.'),
('A deployed update violates a pre-agreed stop condition during its change window. The approved recovery procedure specifies restoring the prior version. Which action follows that plan?', 'Execute the approved rollback when its trigger is met. Continuing a failed rollout despite the stop condition ignores the authorized plan.'),
('A change script completes without error. The service still needs confirmation that intended permissions work and unrelated functions remain available. Which step completes the change?', 'Verify actual outcomes against acceptance criteria. Process completion alone does not establish correct behavior.')])
group(['Teach recognition of warning signs','Rehearse the assigned response roles','Measure behavior after training','Update the material after change'],[
('Employees receive unfamiliar urgent-payment requests and do not know which features indicate possible impersonation. Which awareness activity targets the initial gap?', 'Teach recognition of relevant warning signs and the approved verification process. Measuring behavior before explaining the expectation does not close the knowledge gap.'),
('An incident plan names contacts, but an exercise reveals they do not know their handoff responsibilities. Which training activity is needed?', 'Role rehearsal helps participants practice coordination and handoffs. General phishing awareness does not teach their incident-specific duties.'),
('A campaign has been delivered to all staff. Management wants evidence of improved handling rather than attendance alone. What should be evaluated?', 'Measure appropriate behavior and outcomes using a fair, approved method. Completion counts establish exposure to training, not effectiveness.'),
('A new reporting channel replaces the one shown in every awareness poster. What maintenance action is required?', 'Update the material so employees can follow the current process. Repeating outdated instructions can undermine otherwise effective awareness.')])
group(['Verify the visitor’s authorization','Escort within the approved area','Recover the temporary credential','Review the physical access record'],[
('A vendor arrives at a secure site without appearing on the expected visitor list. The visitor presents a convincing business card. Which step should occur before granting entry?', 'Verify authorization through the site process. A claimed affiliation is not itself permission to enter.'),
('A visitor has been approved to inspect one equipment room under supervision. What control keeps the visit within that authorized scope?', 'Provide the required escort and restrict movement to approved areas. Initial registration does not authorize unrestricted access.'),
('A contractor finishes an approved visit and is leaving with a temporary badge that remains active. Which action closes the temporary access lifecycle?', 'Recover or deactivate the temporary credential according to procedure. A completed visitor log alone may leave the badge usable.'),
('Investigators need to establish whether an authorized technician entered a restricted room during a disputed interval. Which existing evidence is directly relevant?', 'Physical access records can support the timeline, subject to their reliability and limitations. A current badge entitlement does not prove a past entry.')])
group(['Validate the model update','Assign an accountable service owner','Limit the retained training data','Document the automated decision'],[
('An AI-enabled security filter is updated and begins rejecting known legitimate transactions in staging. Which change-control activity should resolve this before promotion?', 'Validate the update against representative acceptance criteria. A model update needs outcome testing just as other security-control changes do.'),
('An automated classification service affects sensitive-data handling, but no team owns its errors, changes or review process. Which governance gap should be closed?', 'Assign accountable ownership for operation and review. A technically accurate model still needs organizational responsibility.'),
('A training pipeline retains personal records that do not contribute to its approved purpose. Which lifecycle change reduces unnecessary privacy exposure?', 'Minimize retained data to the justified purpose and obligations. Better prediction accuracy does not authorize unrelated personal-data retention.'),
('An automated access recommendation influenced a material business decision. Policy requires later explanation of the inputs, version and approving person. Which record is needed?', 'Document the relevant decision provenance and human authorization. A final outcome alone cannot explain how the recommendation was used.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==40
